BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:165437@iso-ne.com
DTSTAMP:20260925T112655Z
DTSTART:20260923T140100Z
SUMMARY:ISO New England to Release the New GridUnity GridInterConnect for Transmission (GIC-T) Application for Account Management ahead of the October 5\, 2026\, Cluster Request Window
DESCRIPTION:You are receiving this message because you are a security administrator or an SA Information Notices contact in the Customer and Asset Management System\, or you have subscribed to the All Notices or Market Notices mailing lists.\n\n\n\nOn September 22\, 2026\, ISO New England released the new GridUnity GridInterConnect for Transmission (GIC-T) application for submitting ISO-administered transmission system interconnection requests. The initial release of the GridUnity GIC-T allows participants to request administrator access for their organizations and set up their company and user records ahead of the October 5\, 2026\, opening of the Cluster Request Window. The next window to submit a complete interconnection request package for the next Cluster Study is expected to be open from October 5\, 2026\, to November 19\, 2026.\n\nThe Interconnection Request Tracking Tool (IRTT) application\, which the GIC-T replaces\, will continue to be available to participants to view information on their interconnection requests submitted on or before June 13\, 2024\, including projects that have completed the Transitional Cluster Study\, a serial system impact study\, or both. Additionally\, the IRTT email address irtt@iso-ne.com will remain available for submitting support questions for both the GridUnity GIC-T and IRTT applications and processes.\n\nVisit the Interconnection Process Guide webpage for details on the interconnection process\, training resources\, and user guides. Check back to the guide for resource updates as the project develops over the coming months.\n\nAdditional Resources:\n\n\n	GridInterConnect for Transmission User Guide\n	Interconnection-related knowledge articles in AskISO.\n	The Cluster Study Participation Forum presentation and recording.\nhttps://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=165437
URL:https://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=165437
END:VEVENT
